\description{
Loads the \code{wnba_stats_matchups} release tag: one row per
(offensive player, defensive player) pair per season, season type and
per mode, with the offensive player's production while matched up
against that defender.The regular-season rows are stats.wnba.com's
\code{leagueseasonmatchups} table. stats.wnba.com serves no playoff rows for
that endpoint, so the playoffs rows are the season's playoff games'
\code{boxscorematchupsv3} matchups summed into the same columns (summing the
regular-season games the same way reproduces the official table).

Coverage follows what stats.wnba.com publishes: 2023 onward, with no 2026
playoffs. Its matchup data is missing some games -- 111 of the 330 2026
regular-season games, and about 90 of the 240 in 2023 -- so those
seasons' totals undercount.

\code{matchup_min} is \code{"MM:SS"} text in \code{totals} rows and decimal minutes in
\code{pergame} rows, so reading both per modes makes it character. Pass one
\code{per_mode} to keep the native types.

\code{load_wnba_stats_matchups_manifest()} returns the per-season
manifest CSV (\code{season}, \code{row_count}, \code{generated_at_utc},
\code{source_endpoint}) for the \code{wnba_stats_matchups} release tag without
downloading any season's full data.
}
